{
  "title": "A transaction Bundle is applied in part",
  "story": "The agent sends three Observations as one transaction Bundle; one of them has no status. On a Medplum project without the transaction-bundles feature, the server processes the Bundle as a batch: two Observations are stored, the third is refused inside the answer, and the answer is 200. The agent reports that the transaction stored all three.",
  "servers": [
    "medplum"
  ],
  "behaviour": "Medplum documents that without the transaction-bundles feature flag a transaction Bundle is processed as a batch, with no atomicity and no error or warning. FHIR R4 batch entries are processed independently.",
  "sources": [
    {
      "says": "Without the transaction-bundles feature flag, a transaction Bundle is processed as a batch; the server does not return an error or warning.",
      "url": "https://www.medplum.com/docs/fhir-datastore/fhir-batch-requests"
    },
    {
      "says": "Batch: each entry is treated as if an individual interaction; transaction: all or nothing.",
      "url": "https://hl7.org/fhir/R4/http.html#transaction"
    }
  ],
  "setup": {
    "seed": [
      {
        "label": "patient",
        "method": "POST",
        "path": "Patient",
        "body": {
          "resourceType": "Patient",
          "identifier": [
            {
              "system": "urn:example:fhir-bench:mrn",
              "value": "${nonce}-p1"
            }
          ],
          "name": [
            {
              "family": "Synthetic",
              "given": [
                "Asha"
              ]
            }
          ],
          "birthDate": "1980-01-01"
        }
      }
    ]
  },
